    fix(server): runtime built-in license URLs are now per-platform, not always OpenAI (#10)
    
    The cockpit hardcodes OPENAI_RUNTIME_URL
    (https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/tools) on every
    "Runtime built-in" license entry, regardless of which platform the
    bundle is being built for. On Claude Code and OpenClaw placards / exports
    this is wrong -- clicking a "Runtime built-in" license card sends users
    to OpenAI's docs when the bundle is actually for Anthropic's Claude Code
    runtime or for OpenClaw.
    
    The BFF now rewrites these URLs based on the placard's (preview) or the
    manifest's (export) platform field:
    
      codex        -> https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/tools   (unchanged)
      claude_code  -> https://code.claude.com/docs/en/tools-reference        (rewritten)
      openclaw     -> https://documentation.openclaw.ai/clawhub/http-api     (rewritten)
    
    The rewrite touches both `license.url` (when `license.source === "runtime"`)
    and any `source_links[].url` that pointed at the OpenAI URL. For exports,
    the LICENSES.md file's inline reference is patched in lockstep so the
    human-readable document stays consistent with the JSON.
    
    Refactor: the existing preview-Gemini-refinement and export-Gemini-rewrite
    blocks were each ungated from `gemini && ...` to just `response.ok && ...`,
    because the runtime URL rewrite should happen even when no Gemini key is
    configured. Gemini calls are still gated on `gemini` being truthy inside
    those blocks. Output is only re-serialized if either step actually
    mutated the JSON.
    
    Also widened `PlacardArtifactSummary` to include the artifact_kind /
    license / source_links fields it always carried at runtime; the previous
    interface was missing them and TypeScript blocked the new helper from
    seeing them.
    
    Verified across all three platforms:
      - codex export: URLs unchanged (codex IS OpenAI's platform)
      - claude_code export: license.url + LICENSES.md both rewritten to the
        Claude Code tools reference
      - openclaw export: license.url + LICENSES.md both rewritten to the
        OpenClaw ClawHub HTTP API docs
      - same per-platform rewriting confirmed on preview placards
    
    All six release gates pass; bundle size unchanged.
    
    Co-authored-by: AnantMirjankar <279104433+AnantMirjankar@users.noreply.github.com>

