    feat(server): have Gemini rewrite the primary instructions file in exports (#9)
    
    After the cockpit returns an /agent-builder/export response, if
    GEMINI_API_KEY is configured the BFF reads
    manifest.file_manifest.instructions (codex-home/AGENTS.md for codex,
    the per-platform equivalent for claude_code / openclaw), sends Gemini
    the user's prompt + that file's current content + the selected
    artifacts, and replaces the file's content with Gemini's rewritten
    version. Stamps `manifest.gemini_instructions` with provenance.
    
    Why: downstream runtimes (Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw) read this file
    to actually build the agent. With cockpit alone, the file is a
    templated stub with the regex-extracted archetype baked in ("Codex
    Customer Support Agent That Reads Agent"). After this change, the file
    opens with a faithful paraphrase of the user's goal, lists the
    artifacts actually present (no inventions), and explicitly calls out
    capability gaps the runtime should ask the user about.
    
    Implementation:
      - New rewriteInstructionsWithGemini() takes prompt, platform,
        current file content, selected_artifacts. Returns the rewritten
        markdown or null on any failure.
      - New ExportShape / ExportManifest interfaces; uses the manifest's
        file_manifest.instructions pointer instead of hardcoding paths,
        so the per-platform indirection works for free.
      - Strips accidental code fences from Gemini output if it wraps.
      - Same safe-fail pattern as the preview rerank: any error -> warn on
        stderr ([gemini rewrite] ...) and return the cockpit's untouched
        response.
    
    Verified end-to-end:
      - Without GEMINI_API_KEY: export returns cockpit's original
        instructions file unchanged; manifest has no gemini_instructions.
      - With bogus GEMINI_API_KEY: real call to Google's API, returns
        API_KEY_INVALID, gracefully falls back, warning logged, original
        file preserved, no gemini_instructions field added.
      - All six release gates pass.
    
    Docs: API.md gains an "Optional Gemini rewrite" subsection describing
    the new manifest.gemini_instructions provenance field and the safe-
    fail semantics.
    
    Co-authored-by: AnantMirjankar <279104433+AnantMirjankar@users.noreply.github.com>

